# The COMPILED catalogue ships; only the sources stay behind.
#
# Round 2 asked for the opposite - translations come from translate.wordpress.org - and the consequence
# was written down at the time: a wordpress.org install has no Bulgarian until the directory has it.
# The directory never got it (api.wordpress.org/translations/plugins/1.0/?slug=bg-couriers answers
# "translations":[]), so from 0.4.26 every wordpress.org shop read the plugin - checkout included - in
# English, while the same code deployed by rsync to our own sites was Bulgarian (shop owner, 2026-10-02).
#
# This is a floor, not a conflict: load_plugin_textdomain() reads wp-content/languages BEFORE the plugin
# folder, so the official pack takes over by itself the day it exists.
languages/*.po
languages/*.pot
test-results
